Regulatory statutes are enacted in conformity with Clause (6) of Article 19 of the Constitution to deal with those trades also which are inherently noxious and pernicious in nature;
and furthermore, thereby sufficient measures are to be taken in relation to health,
safety and welfare of the general public.
